# The engine's own tool-runtime (a `uv sync` derivative of the committed pyproject.toml + uv.lock), the
# platform's per-session worktree directories, and the engine's own regenerable Python bytecode caches —
# kept out of git so they never clutter your repository or your `git status`: the repository-topology rule
# that your own checkout stays a viewing surface rather than a workspace, applied to the engine-managed tool
# runtime, per-session worktree isolation, and the bytecode the engine's tools write under `.engine/` when
# they run (so a read-only diagnostics pass never dirties the tree). This is a single engine-managed block:
# the engine places it and reverses it on removal, so it travels with the template and a generated repo
# ignores these before first-run setup even materializes them. The bytecode line is scoped to `.engine/` so
# the block never reaches into your product's own files.
# BEGIN engine-managed block: foundation-ignores - do not edit inside
.engine/.venv/
.engine/.uv/
.claude/worktrees/
.engine/**/__pycache__/
# END engine-managed block: foundation-ignores

# Python bytecode cache (regenerable; never committed). A general, repo-wide default — it also covers a
# Python PRODUCT built from this template. Unlike the engine-managed fence above it is NOT projected into a
# deployed repo (the fence's `.engine/**/__pycache__/` line ignores only the ENGINE's own bytecode under
# `.engine/`, which is what travels to a brownfield deployment). Ordinary starter hygiene — an adopter may
# keep or drop it; the engine does not manage it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Pytest's run-cache (regenerable; never committed). Mirrors the .engine/.pytest_cache/ carve-out in
# the catalog-coverage check, so a local test run never leaves a stray "surface" directory behind.
.pytest_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store
# BEGIN engine-managed block: core-knowledge-cache - do not edit inside
.engine/knowledge/.cache/
# END engine-managed block: core-knowledge-cache
# BEGIN engine-managed block: core-telemetry-cache - do not edit inside
.engine/telemetry/.cache/
# END engine-managed block: core-telemetry-cache
# BEGIN engine-managed block: memory-substrate-ledger - do not edit inside
.engine/memory/
# END engine-managed block: memory-substrate-ledger
# BEGIN engine-managed block: github-projects-sync-board-config - do not edit inside
.engine/projects-sync/
# END engine-managed block: github-projects-sync-board-config
# BEGIN engine-managed block: core-boot-presentation-ledger - do not edit inside
.engine/boot/.cache/
# END engine-managed block: core-boot-presentation-ledger
# The engine-mechanic's per-machine product-checkout path (eADR-0026): a local pointer to the OWNED product
# repo's clone on THIS machine. Never committed — the product slug travels with the engine, but the local path
# is each maintainer's to set once, so it stays out of git (a whole-directory block, not a lone tracked-surface
# file, so the ownership/surface census never sees it).
# BEGIN engine-managed block: mechanic-product-checkout - do not edit inside
.engine/mechanic/
# END engine-managed block: mechanic-product-checkout
